{"title":"Shaoyi Lai","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Shaoyi Lai","image":"images/profile.png","about":{"template":"trestles","image-shape":"round","image-width":"15em","links":[{"icon":"twitter-x","href":"https://twitter.com/imonimaru"},{"icon":"github","href":"https://github.com/shaoyi-lai"},{"icon":"youtube","href":"https://www.youtube.com/@luasiauiat"},{"icon":"line","href":"https://line.me/ti/p/69aLXk9Uoi"},{"icon":"instagram","href":"https://instagram.com/shaoyi.info"}]}},"headingText":"Education","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nI’m a former public affairs officer with experience in military strategic communications—press releases, print materials, and digital content. I’ve worked with journalists and other communicators to explain defense policy clearly and credibly.\n\nI also research the PRC’s influence operations and information warfare, with a focus on disinformation, narrative strategy, and how public perception shifts in high-stakes geopolitical environments.\n\n📢 Pronounced [Shàoyì](https://voca.ro/12SteQV3fTDZ)\n\nNational Defense University | Taipei, Taiwan M.A. in Journalism | Aug 2014 - Jun 2016\n\nNational Defense University | Taipei, Taiwan B.A. in Journalism | Jan 2008 - Jun 2012\n\n\n\n# Publications {.after-about}\n\n-   **Shu–Min Hou, Wen-Cheng Fu, Shao–Yi Lai**. 2023. “Exploring Information Warfare Strategies during the Russia–Ukraine War on Twitter.” *The Korean Journal of Defense Analysis*, 35(1): pp.19 - 44. [DOI](https://doi.org/10.22883/kjda.2023.35.1.002)\n-   **Su-Yu Chou, Shaoyi Lai**. 2015. “The influence of virtual presence—Internet word-of-mouth and the image of the army in disaster relief.” [*The Third Military News Forum*](https://gpi.culture.tw/books/1010402118).\n-   **Shaoyi Lai, Wenchun Kuo, Jenwei Wei, Chiahou Hung**. 2015. “The current development and future recommendation to the online version of Youth Daily News.” [*The Third Military News Forum*](https://gpi.culture.tw/books/1010402118).\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\nI’m a former public affairs officer with experience in military strategic communications—press releases, print materials, and digital content. I’ve worked with journalists and other communicators to explain defense policy clearly and credibly.\n\nI also research the PRC’s influence operations and information warfare, with a focus on disinformation, narrative strategy, and how public perception shifts in high-stakes geopolitical environments.\n\n📢 Pronounced [Shàoyì](https://voca.ro/12SteQV3fTDZ)\n\n### Education\nNational Defense University | Taipei, Taiwan M.A. in Journalism | Aug 2014 - Jun 2016\n\nNational Defense University | Taipei, Taiwan B.A. in Journalism | Jan 2008 - Jun 2012\n\n\n\n# Publications {.after-about}\n\n-   **Shu–Min Hou, Wen-Cheng Fu, Shao–Yi Lai**. 2023. “Exploring Information Warfare Strategies during the Russia–Ukraine War on Twitter.” *The Korean Journal of Defense Analysis*, 35(1): pp.19 - 44. [DOI](https://doi.org/10.22883/kjda.2023.35.1.002)\n-   **Su-Yu Chou, Shaoyi Lai**. 2015. “The influence of virtual presence—Internet word-of-mouth and the image of the army in disaster relief.” [*The Third Military News Forum*](https://gpi.culture.tw/books/1010402118).\n-   **Shaoyi Lai, Wenchun Kuo, Jenwei Wei, Chiahou Hung**. 2015. “The current development and future recommendation to the online version of Youth Daily News.” [*The Third Military News Forum*](https://gpi.culture.tw/books/1010402118).\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":f